            <div id="metadata" style="display: none;"><div data-category="settings" data-key="shell style" data-value-type="json">"boxed"</div></div>
            <div id="document"><h2>Axioms, Definitions, and Assumed Theorems</h2>
<p>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare and,or, not, implies, contradiction, exists, -,+,leq, =, &lt;,0,1, *, forall&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare and, or, </span><span class="ML__ams">¬</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">⇒</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">→←</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text">and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Equations Rule</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;EquationsRule&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">EquationsRule</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p><strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;SubsRule&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Substitution </span></span></span></span></span>Rule&nbsp;</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Substitution</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;w=v&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">v</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;𝜆P(w)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;𝜆P(v)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">v</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>&nbsp;and-</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W and V&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude </em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;W&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span><br>Conclude <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;V&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;V&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p style="text-align: left;"><strong>and+</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;V&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
</div>
<p style="text-align: left;"><em>Conclude</em>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W and V&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot; W\\text{ and } V&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>or- (proof by cases)</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W or V&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W implies U&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span><span class="ML__cmr">⇒</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">U</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;V implies U&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span><span class="ML__cmr">⇒</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">U</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p>Conclude <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;U&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;U&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">U</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>not+ (proof by contradiction)</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume W&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\rightarrow\\leftarrow&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">→←</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p>Conclude <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not W&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\neg W&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>not- (proof by contradiction)</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume not W&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume not </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">→←</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;Conclude <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;W&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>implies+</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume W&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;V&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;V&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W implies V&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot; W\\Rightarrow V&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span><span class="ML__cmr">⇒</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>contradiction+</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not W&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p>Conclude&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;→←&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\rightarrow\\leftarrow&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">→←</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>exists+</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;𝜆P(t)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.61508em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;exists x.𝜆P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>exists-</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;exists x.𝜆P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;𝜆P(c) for some c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong style="font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, 'Open Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;">forall+</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(a variable declaration)</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;𝜆P(z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall x.𝜆P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>forall-</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall x.𝜆P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;𝜆P(t)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.61508em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Real Numbers:&nbsp;</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Additive Identity </strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+0=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0+x=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>Only one rule is necessary but this is convenient to avoid using substitution with commutativity</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Additive inverse</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+(-x)=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-x+x=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>Only one rule is necessary but this is convenient to avoid using substitution with commutativity</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Multiplicative inverse</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if x neq 0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; then&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x*x^(-1)=1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(x^(-1))*x=1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.864108em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size1">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size1">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>Only one rule is necessary but this is convenient to avoid using substitution with commutativity</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Inverse Equality</strong></p>
<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x^(-1)=1/x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>This rule is unnecessary since any fraction can just be written as a product but this rule makes the proof easier to read.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (associativity of addition)&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 2; text-align: left;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(x+y)+z = x+(y+z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (commutativity of addition)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+y=y+x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (associativity of multiplication)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(x*y)*z=x*(y*z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.63889em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.63889em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (distributive property of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\cdot&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span></span></span></span></span> over <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;+&quot;" data-metadata_given="false"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span>)</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p style="line-height: 2;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x*(y+z)=x*y+x*z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (multiplicative Identity)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x*1=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1*x=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>Only one rule is necessary but this is convenient to avoid using substitution with commutativity</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (multiply by 0)</strong></p>
<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0*x=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Axioms for&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span></span></span></span></span>-These are the 5 axioms selected to define <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span></span></span></span></span>. We then define <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;&lt;&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span></span></span></span></span> in terms of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span></span></span></span></span>. In Theorems 2-6 we show that these axioms are logically equivalent to a set of axioms for <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;&lt;&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Antisymmetric</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x leq y, y leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x=y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Total</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq y or y leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Closure of Non-Negatives Under Multiplication</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If 0 leq x, 0 leq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq x*y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Transitivity</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x leq y, y leq z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Translation</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x leq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+z leq y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Less than</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m&lt;n equiv m leq n,m neq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (DeMorgan's Law)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If neg(W or V or U)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__ams">¬</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">U</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;neg W&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">¬</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span> ,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;neg V&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">¬</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.23em;">V</span></span></span></span></span> , and&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;neg U&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">¬</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">U</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare AlgebraRule, Arithmetic, QQ,  in, NN, is, ^,factorial, sum, infinity, ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare AlgebraRule, Arithmetic, </span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__text">, is, </span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.81em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.39em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">∧</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__text">, factorial, sum, </span><span class="ML__cmr">∞</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text">and </span></span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span></div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;AlgebraRule&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">AlgebraRule</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Arithmetic(QQ)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Arithmetic</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.16667em; height: 0.85556em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>reflexivity&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;W=W&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">W</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Natural Numbers</strong></p>
</div>
<div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>0 is Natural</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:"><strong>Non-Negative Integer</strong><br><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in ZZ, 0 leq x equiv x in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (1 is Natural)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1 in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Factorial Base Case</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0!=1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0!</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Factorial Recursive</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(k+1)!=(k+1)*k!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;k!=(k-1)!*k&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>-In order to keep the rules and proofs clean, we do not specify that this rule only applies for natural numbers, but we ensure we only apply this rule when appropriate.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Natural Number Exponentiation (recursion)</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 2;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z^(n+1)=z*z^n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.72em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Induction:</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(0)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let k be such that k in NN and @P(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__text"> be such that </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(k+1)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot; @P(n)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div><strong>Closure of Integers:&nbsp;</strong></div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Closure of addition on </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{Z}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>)</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x in ZZ, y in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+y in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Closure of </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{Z}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span><strong> Under Multiplication)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x in ZZ, y in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x*y in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (!/!)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If b leq a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a!/b! in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.2em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div><strong>Summation</strong>-These are the selected axioms for summation. Note that lurch treats infinity as a constant that can be substituted for a variable. As such, these rules apply to both infinite and finite summations. This is in line with what Fourier's understanding of finite and infinite summations.&nbsp;
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Sum of 0</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=x to y of 0=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.7em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.34em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Base Case</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=x to x of @P(k)=@P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Splitting Axiom</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to b of @P(k)=sum k=a to x of @P(k)+sum k=x+1 to b of @P(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.84em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.84em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>This rule is only true when <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;a \\leq x \\leq b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span> but we do not type-check this within the rule itself to avoid complications, especially for infinite summations.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Additive Inequality</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If forall k. @P(k) leq @Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__cal">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to y of @P(k) leq sum k=a to y of @Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.7em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.34em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.7em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.34em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cal">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>(<strong>Wait for substitution within summation to be implemented, all theorems)</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n!*(sum k=0 to n of 1/k!)= sum k=0 to n of n!/k!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.302113em; height: 2.9535100000000005em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=0</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size4">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=0</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.2em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m!*(sum k=m+1 to infinity of 1/k!)=sum k=0 to infinity of m!/(m+1+k)!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.360444em; height: 3.0118410000000004em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">∞</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size4">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=0</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">∞</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.2em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 1em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=0 to infinity of (1/(m+1))^(k+1)=(1/(m+1)) * (sum k=0 to infinity of (1/(m+1))^k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=0</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">∞</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.7693300000000001em; height: 1.91377em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size3">(</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.73em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size3">)</span></span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.67em;"><span style="top: -4.17em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.7693300000000001em; height: 1.91377em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size3">(</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.73em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size3">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.302113em; height: 2.9680210000000002em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=0</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">∞</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.7693300000000001em; height: 1.91377em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size3">(</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.73em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size3">)</span></span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.67em;"><span style="top: -4.17em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size4">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p style="line-height: 2;">&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Closure of Positives:</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Closure of positives Inverse)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If 0&lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span><strong> then </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0&lt; 1/x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Closure of Non-Negatives Under Inverse)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If 0 leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq x^(-1)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Inequality Multiplication)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x &lt; y, p leq q, 0&lt;x, 0&lt;y,0&lt;p,0&lt;q&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">q</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text">and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">q</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x*p&lt;y*q&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">q</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Third-of-a-Pound Burger)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x &lt; y, 0&lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1/y &lt; 1/x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.63em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Positive Exponentiation)</strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If 0&lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0&lt;x^y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.72em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Positive Factorial)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0&lt;x!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:"><strong>Theorem(Positive Fraction)</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If 0&lt;p, 0&lt;q&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">q</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0&lt;p/q&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.02em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.63em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">q</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.58em;"><span style="height: 0.63em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare rational, irrational, e&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare rational, irrational, </span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text">and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
<h1><strong>Basic Definitions:&nbsp;</strong></h1>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Def of Integer</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If p in NN, q in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">q</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then<strong> </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p-q in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">q</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Def of Rational</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x is rational&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is rational</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x=m/n, 1 leq n for some m, n in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Def of Irrational</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x is irrational equiv x is not rational&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is irrational</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is not rational</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Def of e</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;e=sum k=0 to infinity of 1/k!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=0</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">∞</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<h1><strong>Closure:</strong></h1>
<p>The following lemmas all trivially follow from closure by induction</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Closure of Negation on </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{Z}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>)</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span><strong> </strong>then<strong> </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-x in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span><strong> &nbsp;</strong></p>
</div>
<h1><strong>Assumed Lemmas:&nbsp;</strong></h1>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Natural Factorial)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x in ZZ, 0 leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x! in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Geometric Series Formula)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=0 to infinity of m^k=1/(1-m)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=0</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">∑</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">∞</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.9em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.73em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (No Integer Between Consecutive Integers)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n&lt;x, x&lt;n+1, n in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text">and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x notin ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∉</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p></div>
        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>math/examples/research/Axioms - Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
            <div id="document"><h2>Theorems</h2>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 1</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x neq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume x neq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will show by contradiction that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;y \\neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume y=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x=y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. However, we already assumed that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x neq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. Thus, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 2 (Trichotomy)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x=y or x&lt;y or y&lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will prove this theorem by contradiction. Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;assume not(x=y or x&lt;y or y&lt;x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">assume not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7335400000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. By DeMorgan's Law,&nbsp;we know that&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;neg(x=y)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">&not;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.625em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;neg(x&lt;y)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">&not;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7335400000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>, and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;neg (y &lt;x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">&not;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7335400000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. The total axiom for less than or equal to states that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq y or y leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. We will now use by a proof by cases to show we have a contradiction.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>First, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;assume x leq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x &lt;y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. However, we have already asserted that&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not(x&lt;y)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7335400000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. Thus, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq y implies contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&rArr;&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>Next, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;assume y leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">assume </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y &lt; x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. However, we already have asserted that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not (y&lt;x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7335400000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. Thus,<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y&le;x&rArr;&rarr;&larr;&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&rArr;&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Therefore, since both cases lead to a contradiction, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, we can conclude the opposite of our initial assumption<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x=y or x&lt;y or y&lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 3 (&lt; is irreflexive)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not(x&lt;x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.0391em; height: 0.5782em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will once again prove this theorem by contradiction.&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume x &lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. However, we know by reflexivity that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. Therefore, we have shown a contradiction, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not( x&lt;x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.0391em; height: 0.5782em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 4 (&lt; is transitive)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x&lt;y, y&lt;z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x&lt;z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume x&lt;y, y&lt;z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y leq z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>, and by transitivity of less than or equal to, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will now show that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;x \\neq z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> by contradiction. Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;assume x=z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>. Then it must be true that&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z&lt;y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z leq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. Therefore, since <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y leq z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z leq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>, it must be true that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z=y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. However, we already know that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z neq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. Therefore,<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x neq z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x &lt;z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 5 (&lt; Translation)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x&lt;y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+z&lt;y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume x &lt;y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x +z leq y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> by the translation axiom for less than or equal to.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will now show that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;x+z \\neq y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> with a proof by contradiction. Therefore, assume that opposite, that is,&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;assume x+z=y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>It follows that,&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x=x+0\n=x+(z-z)\n=(x+z)-z\n=(y+z)-z\n=y+(z-z)\n=y+0\n=y\n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 5.35em;"><span style="top: -7.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 5.35em;"><span style="top: -7.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span><span style="top: -6.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -4.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span><span style="top: -1.5em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: 0;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span><span style="top: 1.49em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">However, we already know that&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. Thus, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+z neq y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+z &lt;y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 6 (Product of Positives)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If 0&lt;x, 0&lt;y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0&lt;x*y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume 0&lt;x, 0&lt;y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> (<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x neq 0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span>), <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 neq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> ( <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y neq 0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span>),&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>, and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. By the axiom for closure of non-negatives under multiplication, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq x*y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will now show that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;0 \\neq x \\cdot y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> by contradiction. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume 0=x*y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>Thus,&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0=0*y^(-1)\n=(x*y)*y^(-1)\n=x*(y*y^(-1))\n=x*1=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 3.89em;"><span style="top: -6.02em;"><span style="height: 1.53em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 3.89em;"><span style="top: -6.02em;"><span style="height: 1.53em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style="top: -4.49em;"><span style="height: 1.53em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.63889em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style="top: -2.97em;"><span style="height: 1.53em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 1.058548em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size1">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size1">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -1.47em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span><span style="top: 0.03em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. However, we have already asserted that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. Thus, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 neq x*y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 &lt; x*y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 7 (Trichotomy(alternate))</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If not(x leq y)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8304100000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y &lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume not(x leq y)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8304100000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. We know that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq y or y leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will now show that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;y \\neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> by contradiction. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume y=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not(x leq x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.13597em; height: 0.7719400000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>. Therefore, we have shown a contradiction, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y neq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y &lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 8 (<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq + &lt;&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span></span></span></span></span>)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If y&le;x, a&lt;b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span><strong> </strong>then<strong> </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y +a &lt; x+b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" title="Good work!" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:" data-validation_result="valid">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume y leq x , a&lt;b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" title="Good work!" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="" data-validation_result="valid">
<p>We will show by contradiction that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;x+b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span> is not less than or equal to <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;y+a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span>. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume x+b leq y+a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp; Since <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;y \\leq x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>, it follows that <span class="lurch-atom" title="Good work!" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y +a leq x+a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom-suffix"><span class="feedback-marker-valid">&nbsp;</span></span></span> by translation.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;x+b \\leq x+a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Thus, &nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;b=b+0\n=b+(x-x)\n=(b+x)-x\n=(x+b)-x\nleq (x+a)-x\n=(a+x)-x\n=a+(x-x)\n=a+0\n=a\n&lt;b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 7.6em;"><span style="top: -9.76em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 7.6em;"><span style="top: -9.76em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span><span style="top: -8.26em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -6.76em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span style="top: -5.26em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.76em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span style="top: -2.25em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span style="top: -0.75em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: 0.75em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span><span style="top: 2.25em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span style="top: 3.74em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom-suffix"><span class="feedback-marker-valid">&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>
<p>However, no number is less than itself so <span class="lurch-atom" title="Good work!" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not (b&lt;b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.0391em; height: 0.73354em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom-suffix"><span class="feedback-marker-valid">&nbsp;</span></span></span>. Thus, we have shown a contradiction, <span class="lurch-atom" title="Good work!" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;contradiction&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&rarr;&larr;</span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom-suffix"><span class="feedback-marker-valid">&nbsp;</span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" title="Good work!" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not (x+b leq y+a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8888799999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom-suffix"><span class="feedback-marker-valid">&nbsp;</span></span></span>. Therefore, it follows that <span class="lurch-atom" title="Good work!" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y+a &lt;x+b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom-suffix"><span class="feedback-marker-valid">&nbsp;</span></span></span> , as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 9 (Inequality Equivalence)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m leq n equiv  exists k.0 leq k and m+k=n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">&equiv;&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">&exist;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p>We will begin by proving the right side of the equivalence implies the left side.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume exists k.0 leq k and m+k=n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__cmr">&exist;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>. Then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq k and m+k=n for some k&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span> . By adding <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span> to each side&nbsp; of &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq k&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;by translation yields, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0+m leq k+m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span>. Since <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0+m=m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m leq k+m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>. Further, we know that addition is commutative&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;k+m=m+k&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp; it&nbsp;follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m leq m+k&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>. Recall that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m+k=n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>. Therefore,&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>We will now show that the left side of the equivalence implies the right side.&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume m leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>. Utilizing translation, subtract <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span> from each side yielding, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m-m leq n-m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
<p>Since&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m-m=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq n-m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Further,</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><br><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;m+(n-m)=m+(-m+n)\n=(m+-m)+n\n=0+n\n=n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 3.11em;"><span style="top: -5.26em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 3.11em;"><span style="top: -5.26em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.76em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span style="top: -2.26em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span style="top: -0.76em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq n-m and m+(n-m)=n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;exists k. 0 leq k and m+k=n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&exist;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 10 (Translation Corollary)</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If 0&lt;x-y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y&lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume 0&lt;x-y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. By translation it follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0+y &lt; (x-y)+y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. By the additive identity <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0+y=y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>, so it follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y &lt; (x-y)+y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>. Further, by associativity and additive inverse,&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(x-y)+y=x+(-y+y)\n=x+0\n=x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 2.36em;"><span style="top: -4.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 2.36em;"><span style="top: -4.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span><span style="top: -1.51em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y&lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 11 (</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq + \\leq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span></span></span></span></span>)</p>
<p>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x leq y, z leq w&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+z leq y+w&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x leq y, z leq w&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span></span></span></span></span>. By translation, it follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+z leq y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z+y leq w+y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>. We know that addition is commutative so <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z+y=y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;w+y=y+w&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span></span></span></span></span>. Then ,<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y+z leq w+y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y+z leq y+w&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>. Therefore, it follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x+z leq y+w&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">w</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 12</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 neq n+1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will be proving this by contradiction so <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;assume 0=n+1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">assume </span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span>. Since we know that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0-1=-1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;1</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n=n+0\n=n+(1-1)\n=(n+1)-1\n=0-1\n=-1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 3.86em;"><span style="top: -6.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 3.86em;"><span style="top: -6.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span><span style="top: -1.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span><span style="top: -0.01em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><br></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">However, since <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;n \\in \\mathbb{N}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>, and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-1 &lt; 0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom-suffix"><span class="feedback-marker-valid">&nbsp;</span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by arithmetic&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by arithmetic</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq n\n=-1 \n&lt; 0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 2.36em;"><span style="top: -4.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 2.36em;"><span style="top: -4.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;1</span></span></span><span style="top: -1.51em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><br>However, no number is less than itself so&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;not(0&lt;0)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">not </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.0391em; height: 0.68354em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. Therefore, we have reached a contradiction.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>It must then be true that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 neq n+1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 13</strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x=y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x-y=z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If x=y+z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>. We can subtract <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> from each side of the equation, producing <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x-y=(y+z)-y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span>.By commutativity, it is obviously true that&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(y+z)-y=(z+y)-y&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span></span> and by associativity &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(z+y)-y=z+(y-y)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. Finally,</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;z+(y-y)=z+0\n=z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.6em;"><span style="top: -3.76em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.6em;"><span style="top: -3.76em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span><span style="top: -2.25em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Therefore,&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x-y=(y+z)-y\n=(z+y)-y\n=z+(y-y)\n=z+0\n=z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 3.86em;"><span style="top: -6.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 3.86em;"><span style="top: -6.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.01em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -1.51em;"><span style="height: 1.5em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span><span style="top: -0.01em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">So <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x-y=z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 14</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If forall k. P(k) &lt; Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to infinity of P(k) &lt; sum k=a to infinity of Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If forall k. P(k) &lt; Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;P(x) &lt; Q(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>, and by the definition of less than or equal to,&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;P(x) leq Q(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>Therefore, since we have shown this is true for an arbitrary <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall k. P(k) leq Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Using the splitting axiom and commutativity of addition</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to infinity of P(k)= sum k=a to a of P(k) + sum k=a+1 to infinity of P(k)\n=P(a)+sum k=a+1 to infinity of P(k)\n=(sum k=a+1 to infinity of P(k))+P(a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 5.12em;"><span style="top: -7.21em;"><span style="height: 3.32em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 5.12em;"><span style="top: -7.21em;"><span style="height: 3.32em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.9em;"><span style="height: 3.32em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -0.49em;"><span style="height: 3.12em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.360444em; height: 3.0118410000000004em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size4">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to infinity of Q(k)= sum k=a to a of Q(k) + sum k=a+1 to infinity of Q(k)\n=Q(a)+ sum k=a+1 to infinity of Q(k)\n=(sum k=a+1 to infinity of Q(k))+Q(a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 5.12em;"><span style="top: -7.21em;"><span style="height: 3.32em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 5.12em;"><span style="top: -7.21em;"><span style="height: 3.32em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.9em;"><span style="height: 3.32em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -0.49em;"><span style="height: 3.12em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.360444em; height: 3.0118410000000004em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size4">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>We know by assumption that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;P(a)&lt;Q(a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. And since we showed that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\forall k. P(k) \\leq Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">)</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">)</span></span></span></span></span>, by the additive inequality axiom it follows that, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a+1 to infinity of P(k) leq sum k=a+1 to infinity of Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>. Using these two in</p>
<p>equalities we can determine that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(sum k=a+1 to infinity of P(k))+P(a) &lt; (sum k=a+1 to infinity of Q(k))+Q(a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.360444em; height: 3.0118410000000004em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size4">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.360444em; height: 3.0118410000000004em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size4">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> by theorem 8. And finally, using the two transitive chains above,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to infinity of P(k) &lt; (sum k=a+1 to infinity of Q(k))+Q(a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.360444em; height: 3.0118410000000004em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.55em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size4">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to infinity of P(k) &lt; sum k=a to infinity of Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>, as desired.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If forall k. @P(k) &lt; @Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__cal">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to infinity of @P(k) &lt; sum k=a to infinity of @Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cal">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 15</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If forall k. 0&lt;1/k!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0&lt; sum k=a to infinity of 1/k!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Assume forall k.  0&lt; 1/k!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Assume </span><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. It directly follows from from the additive inequality axiom that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to infinity of 0&lt; sum k=a to infinity of 1/k!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. However, we know from the base case for infinity summation that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=a to infinity of 0=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span>. Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0&lt; sum k=a to infinity of 1/k!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem 16 (Summation Inequality)</strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If forall k. P(k) leq Q(k), exists z. P(z) &lt;Q(z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&exist;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=x to infinity of P(k) &lt;sum k=x to infinity of Q(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">&infin;</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If forall k. P(k) leq Q(k), exists z. P(z) &lt;Q(z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">&forall;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&exist;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;By the definition of exists,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;P(z) &lt;Q(z) for some z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">Q</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Using the facts that&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=z to z of P(k)=P(z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;sum k=z to z of Q(k)=Q(z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><spa